Simplest robust fix: widen the window *forward* only until the first `;` or `"` closing the field, and backward to the previous `"` field start. Let me implement:

```python
def local_clause(unit, token_line, direction_word):
    i = unit.find(token_line)
    j = token_line.lower().find(direction_word)
    pos = i + j
    # backward: to previous quote/comma/newline/brace boundary
    lo = max(unit.rfind(ch, 0, pos) for ch in ('"', '\n', '{', ',')) + 1
    # forward: to next field terminator
    hi = pos
    for k in range(pos, len(unit)):
        if unit[k] in ';\n':
            hi = k; break
        if unit[k] == '"' and k > pos and unit[k-1] != '\\':
            hi = k; break
    else:
        hi = min(len(unit), pos + 300)
    return " ".join(unit[lo:hi].split())
```

